Export corecrypto symbols CommonCrypto and coretls need for the dyld shared cache.

dyld's shared-cache builder binds every two-level import eagerly, so each symbol
libcommonCrypto.dylib and libsystem_coretls.dylib import from libcorecrypto.dylib
must be exported. corecrypto defines all of these in src/ (chacha20, cmac, dh, ec,
rsa, zp, hkdf, h2c) but left them out of scripts/exported-symbols.exp, so the builder
rejected the cache on dangling imports (the runtime loader tolerated them lazily).
Append the full set as an export block; append is duplicate-safe (a symbol also present
as a commented line stays commented, only the active line exports it).

Signed-off-by: Niclas Overby <niclas@overby.me>
---
--- a/scripts/exported-symbols.exp
+++ b/scripts/exported-symbols.exp
@@ -591,3 +591,24 @@
 
 # not in standard corecrypto, for some reason?
 _ccn_shift_left
+
+# cider #11 A: corecrypto symbols commonCrypto + coretls import for the dyld shared cache.
+# Defined in src/ but were unexported; the shared-cache builder binds these eagerly.
+_ccchacha20
+_ccchacha20poly1305_info
+_ccchacha20poly1305_encrypt_oneshot
+_ccchacha20poly1305_decrypt_oneshot
+_cccmac_cbc
+_ccdh_ccn_size
+_ccdh_gp_g
+_ccdh_gp_n
+_ccdh_gp_prime
+_ccec_blind
+_ccec_unblind
+_ccec_generate_blinding_keys
+_ccrsa_ctx_private_zp
+_cczp_n
+_cczp_prime
+_cch2c
+_cchkdf_extract
+_cchkdf_expand
